      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested** — See inline comments for details.\n\n### Review Summary\n* **Functionality:** `fp_command_template_v0` properly blocks legacy v0 template uploads with `EC_HOST_CMD_ACCESS_DENIED` at entry when `fingerprint_auth_enabled()` is true.\n* **Architecture \u0026 Component Fit:** Placing the `fingerprint_auth_enabled()` guard at the beginning of `fp_command_template_v0` aligns with the existing fingerprint auth command handlers.\n* **Code Simplicity:** In `zephyr/test/fingerprint/task/src/fpsensor_template.cc`, calling `reset_session()` in `fpsensor_before()` clears `FP_ENC_STATUS_SEED_SET` and wipes `global_context.tpm_seed`, which forced moving `fp_seed_params` and `ec_cmd_fp_seed()` out of `fpsensor_setup()` to re-seed the TPM before every test case. Clearing `FP_CONTEXT_STATUS_SESSION_ESTABLISHED` directly (`global_context.fp_encryption_status \u0026\u003d ~FP_CONTEXT_STATUS_SESSION_ESTABLISHED;`) avoids modifying `fpsensor_setup()` or calling `reset_session()`.\n* **Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability:** In `zephyr/test/fingerprint/task/src/fpsensor_template.cc`, `void reset_session(void);` introduces a `.cc` forward declaration with a C-style `(void)` parameter list. Clearing `FP_CONTEXT_STATUS_SESSION_ESTABLISHED` directly eliminates the need for this declaration.\n* **Security:** Blocking unauthenticated v0 template modification paths when fingerprint auth is active prevents arbitrary template injection and forces template operations through the v1 channel.\n* **Testing:** Both `test_fp_command_template_v0_disabled_under_auth` (`fpsensor_auth_commands.cc`) and `test_fp_template_v0_disabled_under_auth` (`fpsensor_template.cc`) verify that v0 requests are rejected with `EC_RES_ACCESS_DENIED` when fingerprint auth is enabled.\n* **CL Size \u0026 Scope:** `Size: M (+58, -8)` (9 production lines and 57 test lines). Tightly scoped to a single logical security change and its unit tests.\n* **Commit Message:** Accurately and concisely explains the security rationale and change.\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/b88d3d29-195f-4ad9-ad38-4a5781efe861)",
